From 13205355aba5671a8074e57fd1a5580b5fc563bf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:43:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): narrow create_overlap target veto to repo, host,
 process [daveey]

Review of 9f7b233331 (PR 387, opus reviewer, probes in hub
~/.hermes/cache/scratch/review387/) replayed the veto over the live hub
replica: it admitted 477 open-card title-matched pairs, among them 71
pairs identical but for a ticket number (BB-434/463/498/...: "Upkeep
failing: assets-health"), i.e. repeat filings of one failing check,
the duplicates this guard exists for.

Why: the ticket class (ABC-123, #123) treated any differing ticket as a
different target. The audit's BB-1155 case is a host difference (mini
vs metta3), so the class was never needed. Also over-broad: host parts
of hyphenated tokens (mini-batch, sx-heart-room-mini), worker-N lanes,
`gateway 8080 port`, a repo named only in both bodies, an inversion
word anywhere in a title, and waits_on matching negated waits ("do not
wait on t_x"), sentence-crossing bridges and producer/parent mentions.

Fix: drop the ticket class; hosts are whole tokens (aliases, gateway
names, metta/gpu/bb-linux N); process is gateway|pid N, not a port; a
repo veto needs one title to name a repo; a revision veto needs the
inversion word next to a word the other title names; waits_on needs an
unnegated park/wait/blocked/depend on <id> within one clause. The new
card's identity is computed once per find, only for title-matched
cards, bodies scanned to 20 KB. Admitted look-alikes are logged.

Live hub replica after: 2 open-pair vetoes (mini vs macbook, mini vs
metta3), both different hosts. Audit replay: all false groups still
admitted, PR181 / v12 / drain owner / Living Room Dot still refused.
Tests: 19 new cases fail on 9f7b233331, all 81 pass.
